# Files that must never reach a deployment.
#
# The CLI already skips `node_modules` and respects `.gitignore` in most cases, but
# "most cases" is not what a secret should depend on: `.env.local` holds the Hotelbeds
# and Ignav keys, and `data/` holds a wholesale rate feed that is not ours to
# redistribute. Both are listed here explicitly so a change to the git rules cannot
# quietly start uploading them.
#
# Every directory is anchored with a leading slash, and that is not cosmetic. A bare
# `data/` also matches any nested directory called `data` — including `src/lib/data/`,
# which is the entire data layer. It broke a build exactly once, in this file, after
# having broken `git add` in `.gitignore` for the same reason.

# Local secrets. Configured in the Vercel dashboard instead, per environment.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Collected hotel prices at the project root (a build artefact, not source).
/data/

# Local caches and build output.
/.cache/
/.npm-cache/
/.next/
/out/
/coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vercel CLI state.
/.vercel/
/.vercel-cli/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
/.idea/
/.vscode/
